WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.910
In Manaus, Brazil, every month
averages 27 to 28 degrees Celsius.

2
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:10.630
Rain totals 2,323 millimetres a year.

3
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.970
Even the driest month gets 68 millimetres.

4
00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:16.530
Here the forest grows in layers.

5
00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:21.390
The tallest trees, the emergents,
stand above a dense roof of leaves.

6
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.930
But dig down, and the soil is
red, and poor in nutrients.

7
00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:30.250
So how can such poor soil
grow such a huge, rich forest?

8
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.530
In this mission, you'll
map where rainforests grow,

9
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.830
and see why they stay
hot and wet all year.

10
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.190
Then you'll follow water
through the forest,

11
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.550
and see how every part of
it depends on the others.

12
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:48.430
Your mission: explain how poor rainforest
soils grow such huge, rich forests.
